The legal text is the Constitution of the State of Minnesota and chapters of Minnesota Statutes (2026 edition), as published by the
Office of the Revisor of Statutes on www.revisor.mn.gov. The pages state no terms of reuse for the text.

Statutes and constitutions are works of government that carry no copyright (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc., 590 U.S. ___, 2020).
The Revisor claims copyright, if at all, only in the arrangement and editorial apparatus of its compilations (headnotes beyond the
statutory text, tables, indexes); this repository takes the section text and the History line of each section, and the Revisor's
amendment notes on the Constitution, and none of the tables or indexes.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication. Source: Office of the Revisor of Statutes, State of Minnesota, www.revisor.mn.gov.
